[158.778554, "o", "\u001b[0m$ \u001b[0msed -n '1,16p' ~/.bashrc; echo '---'; grep -n 'KLEE\\|CPATH\\|PATH' ~/.bashrc | head\r\n# ~/.bashrc: executed by bash(1) for non-login shells.\r\n# see /usr/share/doc/bash/examples/startup-files (in the package bash-doc)\r\n# for examples\r\n\r\n# KLEE (symbolic execution engine) environment\r\nexport PATH=\"/usr/local/bin:$PATH\"\r\nexport CPATH=\"/usr/local/include:/usr/local/include/klee${CPATH:+:$CPATH}\"\r\n\r\n# If not running interactively, don't do anything\r\n[ -z \"$PS1\" ] && return\r\n\r\n# don't put duplicate lines in the history. See bash(1) for more options\r\n# ... or force ignoredups and ignorespace\r\nHISTCONTROL=ignoredups:ignorespace\r\n\r\n# append to the history file, don't overwrite it\r\n---\r\n5:# KLEE (symbolic execution engine) environment\r\n6:export PATH=\"/usr/local/bin:$PATH\"\r\n7:export CPATH=\"/usr/local/include:/usr/local/include/klee${CPATH:+:$CPATH}\"\r\n"]
[159.964551, "o", "> build · deepseek-v4.1-flash\r\n"]
[161.102664, "o", "KLEE is installed and configured.\r\n\r\n**Installed components**\r\n- **STP 2.3.x** (built from source with MiniSat) → `/usr/local/bin/stp`, `/usr/local/lib/libstp.a`\r\n- **KLEE 3.1** (built against LLVM 16, STP solver backend, no uClibc, POSIX runtime disabled) → `/usr/local/bin/klee`\r\n- **KLEE headers** → `/usr/local/include/klee/klee.h`\r\n\r\n**Environment setup in `~/.bashrc`**\r\n```bash\r\nexport PATH=\"/usr/local/bin:$PATH\"\r\nexport CPATH=\"/usr/local/include:/usr/local/include/klee${CPATH:+:$CPATH}\"\r\n```\r\nThese are placed before the non-interactive early return, so they apply even when `~/.bashrc` is sourced non-interactively.\r\n\r\n**Verification**\r\n- Sourcing `~/.bashrc` resolves `klee` to `/usr/local/bin/klee`.\r\n- `klee --version` reports KLEE 3.1 with LLVM 16.\r\n- A test program using `<klee/klee.h>` compiled and ran successfully; KLEE reported `Using STP solver backend` and generated test cases.\r\n- Both `#include <klee/klee.h>` and `#include <klee.h>` work via `CPATH`.\r\n"]
